[63.785377, "o", "  OK      architecture           CPU architecture is x86_64.\r\n  OK      operating system       Operating system is Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS.\r\n  OK      privileges             Running as root, so host changes can be applied.\r\n  OK      cpu                    Host has 4 CPU cores.\r\n  OK      memory                 Host has 15.6 GiB of memory.\r\n  OK      disk                   Root file system has 34.6 GiB free.\r\n  OK      swap                   Swap is disabled.\r\n  OK      cgroups                cgroup v2 is mounted.\r\n  WARN    module overlay         Kernel module \"overlay\" is not loaded. The installer loads it. Tooling is still in the storeroom.\r\n  WARN    module br_netfilter    Kernel module \"br_netfilter\" is not loaded. The installer loads it. Tooling is still in the storeroom.\r\n"]
[63.785446, "o", "  WARN    sysctl                 Sysctl net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables could not be read. The installer sets it after loading br_netfilter.\r\n  WARN    sysctl                 Sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward is \"0\" but \"1\" is required. The installer corrects it.\r\n  WARN    sysctl                 Sysctl net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables could not be read. The installer sets it after loading br_netfilter.\r\n  WARN    containerd             containerd is not installed. The installer installs it from the distribution repository. The machine shop is not equipped yet.\r\n  OK      ports                  All required control-plane ports are free.\r\n  WARN    helm                   helm is not installed. The controller chart cannot be applied until helm is available. The paperwork office is closed.\r\n[2/9] Loading the kernel modules the pod network needs.\r\n"]
[63.786419, "o", "  DRY-RUN would run: write /etc/modules-load.d/brunernetes.conf (21 bytes, mode 0644)\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: modprobe overlay\r\n  OK      Kernel module \"overlay\" is loaded.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: modprobe br_netfilter\r\n  OK      Kernel module \"br_netfilter\" is loaded.\r\n[3/9] Applying the sysctl values required for pod networking.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: write /etc/sysctl.d/99-brunernetes.conf (103 bytes, mode 0644)\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: sysctl --system\r\n  OK      Sysctl values are applied.\r\n[4/9] Installing the pinned Kubernetes packages and the container runtime.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: apt-get update\r\n  OK      Completed: update the package index.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: apt-get install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates curl gpg containerd\r\n  OK      Completed: install the packages needed to add a repository.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c install -m 0755 -d /etc/apt/keyrings && curl -fsSL https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.32/deb/Release.key | gpg --batch --yes --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-ke"]
[63.786461, "o", "yring.gpg && chmod 0644 /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg\r\n  OK      Completed: add the Kubernetes package signing key.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: write /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list (108 bytes, mode 0644)\r\n  OK      Completed: add the Kubernetes package repository.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubelet=1.32.3-1.1 kubeadm=1.32.3-1.1 kubectl=1.32.3-1.1 && apt-mark hold kubelet kubeadm kubectl\r\n  OK      Completed: install the pinned Kubernetes packages.\r\n[5/9] Configuring containerd for the systemd cgroup driver.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c containerd config default\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: write /etc/containerd/config.toml (0 bytes, mode 0644)\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: systemctl restart containerd\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: systemctl enable containerd\r\n  OK      containerd is running with the systemd cgroup driver.\r\n[6/9] Bootstrapping the control plane with kubeadm.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: write /etc/brunernetes/kubeadm.yaml (729 bytes, mode 0600)\r\n  OK      kubeadm c"]
[63.78651, "o", "onfiguration written to /etc/brunernetes/kubeadm.yaml.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: kubeadm init --config /etc/brunernetes/kubeadm.yaml\r\n  OK      Control plane is initialised.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c mkdir -p \"$HOME/.kube\" && cp -f /etc/kubernetes/admin.conf \"$HOME/.kube/config\" && chown \"$(id -u)\":\"$(id -g)\" \"$HOME/.kube/config\"\r\n  OK      Admin kubeconfig copied to $HOME/.kube/config.\r\n[7/9] Preparing the node to run workloads and configuring the pod network.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c KUBECONFIG=/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf kubectl taint nodes --all node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane- --overwrite=false || true\r\n  OK      Control-plane taint removed, so the node runs workloads.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c mkdir -p /opt/cni/bin && curl -fsSL -o /tmp/cni-plugins.tgz https://github.com/containernetworking/plugins/releases/download/v1.6.2/cni-plugins-linux-amd64-v1.6.2.tgz && tar -C /opt/cni/bin -xzf /tmp/cni-plugins.tgz && rm -f /tmp/cni-plugins.tgz\r\n  OK      CNI plugins v1.6.2 installed into /opt/cni/b"]
[63.786631, "o", "in.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: write /etc/cni/net.d/10-brunernetes.conflist (483 bytes, mode 0644)\r\n  OK      Minimal bridge network configuration written to /etc/cni/net.d/10-brunernetes.conflist.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: systemctl restart kubelet\r\n[8/9] Installing the Brunernetes CRDs and controller with Helm.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c KUBECONFIG=/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf helm upgrade --install brunernetes charts/brunernetes --namespace brunernetes-system --create-namespace --wait --timeout 5m\r\n  OK      Brunernetes CRDs and controller are installed in namespace brunernetes-system.\r\n[9/9] Creating the factory resources for the selected preset.\r\n  DRY-RUN would run: bash -c KUBECONFIG=/etc/kubernetes/admin.conf kubectl apply -f -  (with 537 bytes on stdin)\r\n  OK      Factory resources for preset \"garage\" are applied.\r\n\r\nInstallation complete\r\n---------------------\r\nDry run finished. No change was applied to this host. The plan is on the desk, the line has not moved.\r\n"]
